<!--
  Points the compiler's SARIF log at one file per target framework, for harness/linters/dotnet.sh.

  Imported through CustomAfterMicrosoftCommonTargets, which is evaluated after the project body.
  The Props hook the analyzers use is too early: a single-targeted project sets TargetFramework
  in its own body, so at Props time the name below would expand to nothing.

  Two details carry the whole file.

  $(TargetFramework) has to be expanded by MSBuild, once per inner build, which is why the name
  is written here instead of on the command line. MSBuild never re-evaluates a property value
  given with -p:, so on the command line the literal text `$(TargetFramework)` reaches csc and
  every framework of a multi-targeted project writes to the same file: the last writer wins at
  best, two parallel writers interleave into malformed JSON at worst.

  The comma before `version` is written %2c because MSBuild splits the Csc task's ErrorLog item
  spec on an unescaped comma and drops everything after it. Roslyn then falls back to SARIF
  1.0.0, whose result.message is a plain string, and lint/internal/lintfind reads 2.1 only, so
  an unescaped comma turned every report into "malformed JSON" and failed every C# commit.
-->
<Project>
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(TvrmsmithSarifPrefix)' != '' and '$(TargetFramework)' != ''">
    <ErrorLog>$(TvrmsmithSarifPrefix).$(TargetFramework).sarif%2cversion=2.1</ErrorLog>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
